message: "If you use or cite this method, please cite it as below."
title: "Assayance: Falsifiable Assurance — five tests for assurance that can fail"
abstract: >-
  A discipline for testing the instruments of assurance themselves. Core claim:
  a check that has never been observed failing has not been shown to be capable
  of failing, and is therefore not yet a check. Five tests are given — the
  negative control, absence reaching the exit code, the criterion itself under
  test, description as claim, and proxy versus identity judgment — each with a
  recorded instance from the author's own tooling, along with the conditions
  under which the method would be refuted.
type: software
